  <section id="installing-and-approving-extensions">
    <title>Installing and approving extensions</title>
    <p>
      User extensions add personal features, commands, and settings to Orca. Install extension
      files or package directories in ~/.local/share/orca/extensions, or the corresponding
      location under your XDG data directory. Only install code from sources you trust: approved
      extensions run with your user account's permissions.
    </p>
    <p>
      Open User Extensions in the global Preferences window to inspect an extension's
      information and approve it for loading. Changing its code invalidates approval; inspect
      the changes before reapproving it. Revoking approval prevents the extension from loading.
    </p>
    <p>
      Use the switch beside an approved extension to enable or disable it without removing its
      approval. The Settings action opens any preferences provided by the extension. <key>Delete</key> removes the extension file or
      package after confirmation.
    </p>
